WEBVTT

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.000
judysmith: Oh, hey, Whitney.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Whitney Hodges: Hi Judy, how are you?

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.000
judysmith: I'm good. Can you hear me okay?

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Whitney Hodges: I can. Mm-hmm.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.000
judysmith: Okay, good deal.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Are you fine with leaving your camera off today?

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.000
judysmith: I'm sorry, what was that?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Were you going to leave your camera off today or were you trying to get your camera to work too?

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:44.000
judysmith: Oh, I can turn it on. I thought it was on. No, it's fine. Uh… where'd it… up here, yeah.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Whitney Hodges: It's up to you.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.000
judysmith: Well?

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.000
judysmith: Start video.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.000
judysmith: Okay, there it is.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Whitney Hodges: Hi, there you are.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.000
judysmith: Yes, you're right.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Good to see you!

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Whitney Hodges: So, um…

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.000
judysmith: Okay.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Whitney Hodges: We got your changes a couple of days ago for the, um, the ads, the meta ads, so all that should be good. We should be getting that round of meta ads launched very soon, so that's exciting.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.000
judysmith: Right.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.000
judysmith: Okay.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.000
judysmith: All right, good, good.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Whitney Hodges: And then, um, first things first, I wanted to chat with you about the calendar, just to make sure I'm clear on, um, what you're needing, and that you kind of have an understanding of how it typically works.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.000
judysmith: Yeah.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.000
judysmith: Yeah.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:41.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, with LeadLock. I know you had some concerns about how, like, when you synced, um, TeamUp with your Google Calendar, that you could, like, see the couple's names, but with the way that LeadLock works.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.000
judysmith: Right.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.000
judysmith: Uh-huh.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:57.000
Whitney Hodges: potential clients are never gonna see, like, your actual Google Calendar, right? Like, they wouldn't see what's actually listed on the calendar. It's more like with the lead lock calendars, it shows what's available, right?

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.000
judysmith: Oh!

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.000
judysmith: Okay.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.000
judysmith: Just a block.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000
judysmith: Okay, okay, well then that makes sense.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Whitney Hodges: And so, typically, we use the LeadLock calendars just for booking tours, right? Like, we send people a link, and it shows what dates are available for booking tours. But are you thinking that you're wanting to use LeadLock to show people.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:21.000
Whitney Hodges: what wedding dates are available as well, or were you going to continue to use TeamUP for that?

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:26.000
judysmith: Um, that… I thought y'all had said that it would need to go into lead log.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.000
judysmith: And that the calendar.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:44.000
Whitney Hodges: Not necessarily. So, LeadLock is what I would recommend using for booking tours, right? Um, but if you like utilizing TeamUp and are planning to continue to for booking, you know, or blocking the weddings themselves.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.000
judysmith: Okay.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.000
judysmith: Brewers. Okay.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.000
judysmith: Uh-huh.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.000
judysmith: Right.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:03:06.000
Whitney Hodges: I don't necessarily see an issue with that, I don't think. I think what my question is at this point is that I know that typically, like in that initial email that goes out to people, there's usually a PDF, right, that's attached that's being pulled from TeamUP that shows that availability.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.000
judysmith: Yes.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.000
judysmith: Correct.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:20.000
Whitney Hodges: And so I think that's maybe what I want to kind of talk through, like, if that's something that you're wanting to continue to do, because that calendar changes, right? Like, that PDF has to change when your availability changes, right?

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:26.000
judysmith: Right. It can change daily. Yeah. Uhhuh. And so I did not that. Okay, well that is then I guess our big question is how you.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:33.000
judysmith: How will it… how would we change it as on…

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.000
judysmith: Lead lock.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm, yeah, great question. Yeah, so, you know, if we were to kind of continue to do it the way that you're doing it now, right, where there's an attachment that shows the availability.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.000
judysmith: Right.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.000
judysmith: Okay.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.000
judysmith: Bye.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.000
judysmith: Right.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:58.000
Whitney Hodges: Like, we can do that, we can have that attachment live there within the workflows, but basically, every time you book a new wedding, you would have to download a new version of the PDF, right? And then we would have to update that automated email.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.000
judysmith: Uh-huh.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.000
judysmith: Right.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.000
judysmith: Yeah.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:17.000
Whitney Hodges: So, I mean, I think that is doable, but it's also, I mean, it could be a little bit more cumbersome, right, than just an email that exists, and it's always that way, sort of thing. So, I don't know how you feel about that, or how often on your end, really, are you.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.000
judysmith: a lot more…

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.000
judysmith: Perfect.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.000
judysmith: Yes.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.000
judysmith: Yeah.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:21.000
Whitney Hodges: downloading a new version of the PDF to send over to couples.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:28.000
judysmith: Probably we were. Things have dropped off tremendously. Weekly.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.000
judysmith: So, yeah, not like…

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.000
judysmith: every day, but more weekly is what it would be. And.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:40.000
judysmith: So, when… okay, um…

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.000
judysmith: Let's see.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:51.000
judysmith: Yeah, I was just trying to figure out… I kind of had looked at some of the other wedding venues, and I know a lot of them post their calendar.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.000
judysmith: Uh, you know, on their website.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Mm-hmm.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:04.000
judysmith: And so then you can look and see if that date is available. We had not ever done that because you, we were hoping, you know, if your date.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:10.000
judysmith: was not available, then they would maybe pick a different one.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:29.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Exactly. Yeah. And I agree with that. I don't think you should post the full wedding date availability on the website. I think it's kind of something that you want people to ask for sort of thing. You know what I mean? So I think what we can, we can try to do on our end. We haven't done this before, right? So it's going to be a little bit of an experiment.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.000
judysmith: Yeah.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.000
judysmith: Phone.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.000
judysmith: Okay.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.000
judysmith: Yeah, yes, yeah.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.000
judysmith: Okay.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:48.000
Whitney Hodges: But we can try to create a lead block calendar that specifically shows wedding availability, right? And so it would show when a date is already booked, right? But should be able to show what dates are available. Um, and it would be something that, like, couples could kind of click through, like, month by month.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.000
judysmith: Aha.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.000
judysmith: Uh-huh.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.000
judysmith: Right.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:06:01.000
Whitney Hodges: to see what's open. So we can play around with that and, um, see if you like it, kind of see if that works the way that we need it to. But in the meantime, I think let's continue with having the, um.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.000
judysmith: Yeah. Okay.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.000
judysmith: Okay.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.000
judysmith: Works.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.000
judysmith: Right.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:23.000
Whitney Hodges: the, uh, the TeamUP PDFs attached to the emails, and if you guys just want to contact us, you know, or, you know, shoot us an email with new PDFs every time it changes, like when you book something new, we can get that updated. We'll also, once LeadLock is officially up and running for you, we can show you how you can go in and change it yourself.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.000
judysmith: Okay.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.000
judysmith: I'm just…

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:27.000
judysmith: Okay. Okay. All right. So now on the, uh.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:33.000
judysmith: calendar that you will show only lock which is for tours.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:38.000
judysmith: So, we'll… you'll need to kind of get, um, from us…

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:44.000
judysmith: Availability, right? And how will they handle that? Yeah.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.000
Whitney Hodges: Right, yeah, yeah, it'll be perfect to know.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:59.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm. Yeah, so it'll be great to know, just kind of in general, like, I think you've mentioned before that, like, on Saturdays, you usually do tours from 9 to 11, right? Or if there's any other more kind of, like, general hours of when you're hosting tours, we'll definitely want to put that in the system.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.000
judysmith: Right.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.000
judysmith: No.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, what… where LeadLock will be connected is, it'll be connected to your Google Calendar, right? So if there's a conflict on the Google Calendar of a meeting that you already have, or a tour that's already booked, right? People are gonna not see that that time is available for a tour.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.000
judysmith: Right.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.000
judysmith: Okay, okay, okay.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, and if there ends up being something where it's a day where you guys just aren't available for tours at all, or somebody's out of town, or something like that, you can block it one of two ways, right? Like, on your actual Google Calendar, you could just.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.000
judysmith: Right.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.000
judysmith: Right, right.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.000
judysmith: Oh.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:43.000
Whitney Hodges: put a block on that day in its entirety, or it can be done inside of LeadLock as well, so we can kind of show you how to do it either way.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.000
judysmith: Okay.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.000
judysmith: All right.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:49.000
judysmith: Okay, okay, because, yeah, all right, and then I'll make sure Brittany is here when we go over that, too. Yeah, okay.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm. Okay.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:54.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, perfect. Okay. Any other calendar-related questions?

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.000
judysmith: Okay, good.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:58.000
judysmith: And… not that I can think, we'll kind of leave…

