00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:48.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, I think if you probably want to send it to both of us, that would be great.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:56.000
judysmith: Okay. Okay.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:22:00.000
Whitney Hodges: I'm just taking a look here.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:08.000
Whitney Hodges: And I wouldn't say, like, I don't know that I'm seeing anything necessarily out of the ordinary. Um…

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.000
judysmith: Okay. All right.

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:26.000
Whitney Hodges: So when I look here, this is the last 90 days, right? So we can see from, like, July until now, there was a really big spike. I'm not sure what that maybe was attributable to, just one day on August 3rd. But other than that, it seems to be kind of, like.

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.000
judysmith: Yeah.

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.000
judysmith: Bye.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:24.000
judysmith: Oh, good. Okay.

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:33.000
Whitney Hodges: ebbing and flowing and that things are fairly similar from where they've been. Yeah.

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:30.000
judysmith: Okay. Alright.

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:46.000
judysmith: Okay. Yeah. And I mean, uh, right now we're, we, I don't know if it's just us, but I'm, I imagine it's a lot of the wedding industry. We're seeing a significant.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:51.000
judysmith: Uh, drop off in bookings and request for information.

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:52.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.000
judysmith: Yeah.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:23:08.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, I'm definitely hearing from our other venues that things are feeling a little slower right now, in general. That, um, you know, that they're, uh, not as booked out for 2027 as they would normally be this time of year.

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:00.000
judysmith: Yeah.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.000
judysmith: Yeah. Okay.

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:06.000
judysmith: Right.

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:09.000
judysmith: Right.

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:25.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, that they're either seeing couples that are inquiring for super quick turnaround times on, like, they're wanting to have a wedding really soon, or they are touring, but they're looking at dates that are pretty far out, and they're, like, not.

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
judysmith: Yes.

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:20.000
judysmith: Yep.

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:25.000
judysmith: Right.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:31.000
Whitney Hodges: There's no sense of urgency, it seems like, in terms of them kind of making a decision.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:34.000
judysmith: No, and, and another thing, just so, just of a information for y'all.

00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:41.000
judysmith: We have never in 13 years had so many cancellations of weddings that we've had.

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:42.000
Whitney Hodges: Like, actual wedding cancellations?

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:47.000
judysmith: Yeah, we had for this year alone. We have 5 and.

00:23:47.000 --> 00:24:00.000
judysmith: none of them got their money back, and some had to go ahead and pay, uh, pay out what they owed us, because there was really no reason, like, I mean, like, I'm very sensitive to people who…

00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Wow.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:09.000
judysmith: they've gotten ill, or they're having to take care of family, or something, as long as they're, you know, being truthful. But this is just… we're… we're canceling. Yeah.

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:06.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Mm-hmm.

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:16.000
Whitney Hodges: And, like, is it that they're, like, breaking up, or they're like, we just don't want a big wedding anymore, and we're doing it somewhere else? Do you know?

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:23.000
judysmith: I think it's more the cost of, like, they've gotten down to it, especially because food costs have gotten so high.

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:25.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:27.000
judysmith: That they're like, we can't afford it. Yeah.

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, but then they're just completely eating the cost of the venue. That's crazy.

00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:36.000
judysmith: Of us, yeah. Yeah, it's very strange, and… and that's what, um…

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:51.000
judysmith: my husband was just talking yesterday, he said, well, did… were you able to rebook some of them? And I'm like, no, no, and even offering them… yeah, like, because usually what our policy is, is if we can rebook it, we'll refund X amount of your money, you know?

00:24:42.000 --> 00:24:46.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, I wanted that short term.

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:53.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Mm-hmm.

00:24:51.000 --> 00:25:05.000
judysmith: And, I mean, and I've even reached out to planners and offered a big, you know, discount on them. I hadn't been able to, yeah, but I just thought I would pass that information along.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:04.000
Whitney Hodges: Wow.

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:18.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, that is definitely interesting to know. So if they cancel, do you still collect the full amount of what they would owe? Or is it like if they cancel by a certain date, they don't owe the full amount? How does it work?

00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:10.000
judysmith: Yeah, because I think…

00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:16.000
judysmith: Yeah.

00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:26.000
judysmith: Oh, no, if they… if they don't… okay, the cancellation policy is if, um…

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:41.000
judysmith: Okay, if they have not paid everything, then the full amount is due. Usually, I'll let them pay it out, um, and I can apply their refundable security deposit to what they owe. And so, usually, I mean, I'm…

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:40.000
Whitney Hodges: Right.

00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:49.000
judysmith: you know, I don't want to be mean and stuff to them, and so we try to… to… you know, if they owe us maybe…

00:25:49.000 --> 00:26:04.000
judysmith: less than $2,000 I'll let it go, you know, you know, so, and we'll apply their deposit to it. And so that's usually work. But yeah, it's been very, very strange, because, I mean, I think in.

00:25:52.000 --> 00:25:55.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:25:58.000 --> 00:25:59.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:09.000
judysmith: In 13 years, we've only had one person.

00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:12.000
judysmith: Like four cancellations.

00:26:10.000 --> 00:26:14.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, wow, that's wild.

00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:14.000
judysmith: Yeah.

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:27.000
judysmith: Yeah, so it's been a very interesting year, and I do think it's part of the economy and cost of everything. But yeah, I just thought I would kind of let y'all know that bit of information.

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:24.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm, yeah.

00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, no, that's an interesting tidbit, for sure, because I hadn't been hearing that from other venues, but that doesn't mean that it's not happening.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:31.000
judysmith: It… it…

00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:40.000
judysmith: Yeah, yeah, I know. Well, I hope it's not just us. And so, yeah, no, no. And so, yeah, it's very odd. Yeah.

00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:34.000
Whitney Hodges: Mmhm.

00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:37.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:41.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, okay.

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:43.000
judysmith: Bye. Bye. Bye. All right.

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Awesome. Okay. Well, thank you so much for taking the time today. Um, we'll, um, you know, be in touch with… with more on the LeadLock side of things. Um, we'll let you know once those initial meta ads are, uh, officially launched, and there will be more meta.

00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:45.000
judysmith: All right.

00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:50.000
judysmith: Mm-hmm.

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:56.000
judysmith: Okay.

